{#
mail/_attachment_preview.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Reading a PDF attachment without downloading it.

Rendered into the app's modal frame. The document itself is NOT delivered by
this response — the controller fetches the bytes from `app_mail_attachment`,
which is unchanged and still serves them as a download. `fetch()` ignores
Content-Disposition, so the strict inline allow-list stays exactly as strict as
it was.

The panel is `flex flex-col max-h-[92vh] overflow-hidden`, so the page stack
must be `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-auto` or it will not scroll — the same shape
the integration picker uses inside this dialog.

The download link stays. Reading in place is the point of this screen, but a
document you are asked to sign is one you may well want a copy of, and removing
the only way to get one would be a loss dressed as a feature.

TWO CONTROLLERS, ONE ELEMENT
────────────────────────────
mail--pdf-viewer reads; mail--pdf-sign writes on it. They ride the same element
and the signing one talks to the reader through the small surface that
controller marks as its own. Reading is the feature almost everyone will use and
it stays whole, and testable, without any of the signing code — pdf-preview.spec
and pdf-sign.spec are separate for the same reason.

The signature is VISUAL: a picture of a name, stamped on a page. It is not
PAdES, it carries no certificate, and nothing on this screen may suggest it
proves the document is unaltered.
#}
{% set assets  = pdfjs_assets() %}
{% set message = part.message %}

{# A reply opens inline at the foot of the conversation, and falls back to the
   dock for a message that somehow is not threaded — the same choice
   _message_actions makes, and made the same way so the two cannot drift. #}
{% set composeFrame = message.thread is not null ? 'compose_inline' : 'compose_dock' %}
{% set signedName   = (part.filename ?: 'document.pdf')|replace({'.pdf': '', '.PDF': ''}) ~ '-signed.pdf' %}

<turbo-frame id="modal" class="flex-1 min-h-0 flex flex-col">
    <div class="flex-1 min-h-0 flex flex-col"
         data-controller="mail--pdf-viewer mail--pdf-sign"
         data-mail--pdf-sign-action-value="{{ path('app_compose_reply_signed', { id: part.id, frame: composeFrame, thread: message.thread ? message.thread.id : null }) }}"
         data-mail--pdf-sign-token-value="{{ csrf_token('reply_signed' ~ part.id) }}"
         data-mail--pdf-sign-frame-value="{{ composeFrame }}"
         data-mail--pdf-sign-filename-value="{{ signedName }}"
         data-mail--pdf-sign-encrypted-text-value="{{ 'attachment.sign.protected'|trans }}"
         data-mail--pdf-sign-unreadable-text-value="{{ 'attachment.sign.unreadable'|trans }}"
         data-mail--pdf-sign-saved-url-value="{{ app.user.signature ? path('app_settings_profile_signature', { filename: app.user.signature }) : '' }}"
         data-mail--pdf-viewer-src-value="{{ path('app_mail_attachment', { id: part.id }) }}"
         data-mail--pdf-viewer-assets-value="{{ assets|json_encode }}"
         data-mail--pdf-viewer-failed-text-value="{{ 'attachment.preview.failed'|trans }}">

        {# ── Toolbar ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
        <div class="shrink-0 flex items-center gap-3 border-b border-line px-4 py-2">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-file-pdf text-danger shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>

            <span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-ink" title="{{ part.filename }}">
                {{ part.filename ?: 'attachment.preview.untitled'|trans }}
            </span>

            <div class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-1 shrink-0">
                {# Page position. Hidden until the document reports a count, so
                   a failed load does not leave "1 / 0" on screen. #}
                <span data-mail--pdf-viewer-target="pages"
                      class="hidden mr-2 text-xs text-ink-faint tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap"></span>

                {% if app.user.signature %}
                    <button type="button"
                            data-action="mail--pdf-sign#useSaved"
                            class="mr-1 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium
                                   text-ink-soft hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-stamp text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        {{ 'attachment.sign.use_saved'|trans }}
                    </button>
                {% endif %}

                <button type="button"
                        data-action="mail--pdf-sign#open"
                        class="mr-1 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium
                               text-ink-soft hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-signature text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ 'attachment.sign.action'|trans }}
                </button>

                <button type="button"
                        data-action="mail--pdf-viewer#zoomOut"
                        aria-label="{{ 'attachment.preview.zoom_out'|trans }}"
                        class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-muted
                               hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-minus text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </button>

                <button type="button"
                        data-action="mail--pdf-viewer#zoomIn"
                        aria-label="{{ 'attachment.preview.zoom_in'|trans }}"
                        class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-muted
                               hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-plus text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </button>

                {# ?download=1 and the download attribute, both: the query
                   parameter is what makes the server send it as an attachment,
                   and the attribute is what stops Turbo Drive swallowing a
                   non-HTML response. The chip's docblock explains the second. #}
                <a href="{{ path('app_mail_attachment', { id: part.id, download: 1 }) }}"
                   download="{{ part.filename ?: 'attachment.pdf' }}"
                   data-turbo="false"
                   aria-label="{{ 'attachment.preview.download'|trans }}"
                   class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-muted
                          hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-download text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>

        {# ── Pages ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
        <div data-mail--pdf-viewer-target="scroller"
             class="relative flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-auto bg-sunken/40 px-4 py-4">

            <div data-mail--pdf-viewer-target="stack" class="mx-auto flex flex-col items-center gap-4"></div>

            {# The placed signature. A SIBLING of the page stack, not a child of
               it: the reader empties that stack and rebuilds it on every zoom,
               which took the stamp with it. Positioned against the scroller,
               which is why the scroller is `relative` — an absolutely
               positioned child of a scrolling box scrolls with its content, and
               the stamp belongs to the page rather than to the window.

               Dragged by its body, resized by the corner. #}
            <div data-mail--pdf-sign-target="stamp"
                 data-action="pointerdown->mail--pdf-sign#grab
                              pointermove->mail--pdf-sign#drag
                              pointerup->mail--pdf-sign#drop
                              pointercancel->mail--pdf-sign#drop"
                 hidden
                 class="absolute z-20 cursor-move touch-none select-none
                        bg-contain bg-no-repeat bg-center
                        outline outline-2 outline-offset-2 outline-accent/70">
                <span data-resize
                      class="absolute -right-1.5 -bottom-1.5 h-3 w-3 cursor-nwse-resize
                             rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
            </div>

            <div data-mail--pdf-viewer-target="status"
                 class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-2 py-12 text-ink-faint"
                 aria-live="polite">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-notch fa-spin text-2xl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <p class="text-sm">{{ 'attachment.preview.loading'|trans }}</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        {# ── Why it cannot be signed ─────────────────────────────────────── #}
        <p data-mail--pdf-sign-target="reason" hidden
           class="shrink-0 border-t border-line bg-warning-soft px-4 py-2 text-xs text-ink-soft"
           aria-live="polite"></p>

        {# ── The pad ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
        {# Backed at four times the size it is shown at — see the controller.
           touch-none is what stops a finger stroke scrolling the reader
           instead of drawing on it. #}
        <div data-mail--pdf-sign-target="pad" hidden
             class="shrink-0 border-t border-line bg-surface px-4 py-3">

            <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 pb-2">
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted">{{ 'attachment.sign.draw'|trans }}</p>

                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                    <button type="button"
                            data-action="mail--pdf-sign#clear"
                            class="rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover
                                   hover:text-ink transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                        {{ 'attachment.sign.clear'|trans }}
                    </button>

                    <button type="button"
                            data-action="mail--pdf-sign#close"
                            class="rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover
                                   hover:text-ink transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                        {{ 'attachment.sign.cancel'|trans }}
                    </button>

                    <button type="button"
                            data-mail--pdf-sign-target="apply"
                            data-action="mail--pdf-sign#apply"
                            disabled
                            class="rounded-lg bg-accent px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-on-accent
                                   disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed
                                   hover:bg-accent-strong transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                        {{ 'attachment.sign.place'|trans }}
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>

            <canvas data-mail--pdf-sign-target="ink"
                    data-action="pointerdown->mail--pdf-sign#startStroke
                                 pointermove->mail--pdf-sign#stroke
                                 pointerup->mail--pdf-sign#endStroke
                                 pointerleave->mail--pdf-sign#endStroke
                                 pointercancel->mail--pdf-sign#endStroke"
                    class="block h-28 w-full touch-none rounded-lg border border-dashed border-line
                           bg-white cursor-crosshair"></canvas>
        </div>

        {# ── What to do with the signed copy ─────────────────────────────── #}
        {# A real form, submitted by Turbo into the compose frame, so the window
           comes back where it belongs and modal_controller closes the dialog on
           turbo:submit-end without a line of new JavaScript. #}
        <div data-mail--pdf-sign-target="sheet" hidden
             class="shrink-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 border-t border-line px-4 py-3">

            <p class="mr-auto text-xs text-ink-muted">{{ 'attachment.sign.hint'|trans }}</p>

            <button type="button"
                    data-action="mail--pdf-sign#download"
                    class="rounded-lg border border-line px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-ink-soft
                           hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                {{ 'attachment.sign.download'|trans }}
            </button>

            <button type="button"
                    data-action="mail--pdf-sign#reply"
                    class="rounded-lg bg-accent px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-on-accent
                           hover:bg-accent-strong transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                {{ 'attachment.sign.reply'|trans }}
            </button>

            <form data-mail--pdf-sign-target="form"
                  action="{{ path('app_compose_reply_signed', { id: part.id, frame: composeFrame, thread: message.thread ? message.thread.id : null }) }}"
                  method="post"
                  enctype="multipart/form-data"
                  data-turbo-frame="{{ composeFrame }}"
                  hidden>
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('reply_signed' ~ part.id) }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="frame" data-mail--pdf-sign-target="frameField">
                <input type="file" name="document" data-mail--pdf-sign-target="file">
            </form>
        </div>
    </div>
</turbo-frame>
